{{~##
   The module's implementation: the table loads and the accessor's storage. Split from the
   header because a USTRUCT's methods cannot be defined inline in a header UHT parses
   without the definitions landing in every translation unit.

   A table reads column by column, so the loop the record used to own now belongs to the
   table: the file names each column by tag, and the switch below is what decides which
   member it fills - or that nothing here knows it and its bytes are skipped.

   Reads go straight into the members. The reader has an overload per engine type, so
   there is no temporary to declare and no conversion to apply.

   Failure is checked once per table rather than once per field. The reader's failure is
   sticky: the first read that runs out of data records why and the rest do nothing. The
   loops whose trip count came off the wire do look at it mid-flight - a corrupt count
   would otherwise spin appending default elements until the allocator gave up.
##~}}
